  "verdict": "GO",
  "verdict_rationale": "GO: Corrected in-distribution robustness validation confirmed across 168 views and 14 DTU scenes. Heterogeneous convergence is robust and stable: 92.9% of views saturate before K=16 at 5% tolerance (81.0% at 2% tolerance). The scene-wise mean compute savings is 27.5% with 95% bootstrap CI [22.7%, 32.4%], strictly bounded away from zero. Mean intra-scene variance is 2.95, proving per-view heterogeneity is not an artifact of scan selection. Crucially, cheap observable signals demonstrate statistically significant predictive capability for future gain (Spearman rho = 0.621, AUROC = 0.861), providing an empirical foundation for controller design."
